/* book: the chapter, paragraph by paragraph (first sentences):
   - Voltage form: an ideal Vs in series with R.
   - Current form: an ideal Is in parallel with R.
   - The two lines are identical when Vs = IsR.
   - Is = Vs/R (voltage form to current form) and Vs = IsR (current form to voltage form).
   - The direction rule follows from the short-circuit current: shorting the voltage form drives current out of its + terminal and round through the short, so the current source must push current out of the same terminal.
*/
