/* book Worked example: Q: For the bridge circuit of the figure (branch 1: A to B, 20 Ω; 2: A to C, 20 Ω; 3: C to B, 10 Ω; 4: B to D, 2 Ω; 5: C to D, 8 Ω; 6: the 36 V source from D to A), use the tree {4, 5, 6} to write the tie-set equations, find all six branch currents and check them with the cut-set equations.
   1. Loop currents are the link currents I₁, I₂, I₃. From i = Bᵀ IL: i₁ = I₁, i₂ = I₂, i₃ = I₃, i₄ = I₁ + I₃, i₅ = I₂ − I₃, i₆ = I₁ + I₂.
   2. Branch voltages (drop along the arrow): vk = Rkik for the resistors and v₆ = −36 V for the source, since its arrow runs from − to +.
   3. Tie-set 1 (branches 1, 4, 6): 20I₁ + 2(I₁ + I₃) − 36 = 0, so 22I₁ + 2I₃ = 36.
   4. Tie-set 2 (branches 2, 5, 6): 20I₂ + 8(I₂ − I₃) − 36 = 0, so 28I₂ − 8I₃ = 36.
   5. Tie-set 3 (branches 3, 4, −5): 10I₃ + 2(I₁ + I₃) − 8(I₂ − I₃) = 0, so 2I₁ − 8I₂ + 20I₃ = 0.
   6. Solve: I₁ = (36 − 2I₃)/22 and I₂ = (36 + 8I₃)/28. Substituting and multiplying by 308 gives 1008 − 56I₃ − 3168 − 704I₃ + 6160I₃ = 0, so 5400I₃ = 2160 and I₃ = 0.4 A. Then I₁ = 35.2/22 = 1.6 A and I₂ = 39.2/28 = 1.4 A.
   7. Branch currents: i₁ = 1.6 A, i₂ = 1.4 A, i₃ = 0.4 A, i₄ = 2.0 A, i₅ = 1.0 A, i₆ = 3.0 A.
   8. Cut-set check: twig 4: −1.6 − 0.4 + 2.0 = 0; twig 5: −1.4 + 0.4 + 1.0 = 0; twig 6: −1.6 − 1.4 + 3.0 = 0. The same numbers came out of the star-delta reduction of this bridge.
   Answer: i₁ = 1.6 A, i₂ = 1.4 A, i₃ = 0.4 A, i₄ = 2 A, i₅ = 1 A and the source current i₆ = 3 A. */
